717112,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-51131537-88e9-4696-a0bf-4e4f1967ffa2","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office - Policy premium calculation and claim processing\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 29\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should calculate base premium for a single sword -- 100 G\n2. should calculate base premium for a single amulet -- 60 G\n3. should calculate base premium for a single staff -- 80 G\n4. should calculate base premium for a single potion -- 40 G\n5. should calculate base premium for a single component (rune or moonstone) -- 25 G\n6. should calculate base premium for 2 components -- 50 G\n7. should apply building block discount for exactly 3 alike components -- 3 runes → 60 G\n8. should not apply building block discount for 4 alike components -- 4 runes → 100 G\n9. should not apply building block discount for different types of components -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone → 75 G\n10. should apply building block discount to each group of 3 alike components -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G\n11. should add 50% risk surcharge for cursed items -- cursed sword adds 50 G to its base premium\n12. should add 30% risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment level ≥ 5) -- enchanted sword (enchantment 5) adds 30 G to its base premium\n13. should show item-specific modifiers apply only to the affected item's base premium -- cursed sword and plain amulet → only sword's 100 G base is increased by 50%\n14. should apply 20% loyalty discount for long-standing customers (≥ 2 years) -- customer with 2 years → 20% discount on policy base premium\n15. should apply 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance -- first insurance carries 10% surcharge\n16. should apply 15% discount on contracts after the first -- second contract → 15% discount on policy base premium\n17. should apply both loyalty and follow-up discounts correctly -- 3-year customer, second contract, cursed sword → 160 G premium\n18. should add 5 G processing fee to every premium -- empty list → 5 G\n19. should calculate premium for empty item list -- 5 G\n20. should reject quote with unknown item type and exit with non-zero status -- type: broomstick → error\n21. should reject claim with item not part of the policy and exit with non-zero status -- amulet damaged when only sword insured → error\n22. should reject claim with unknown item type in damage and exit with non-zero status -- unknown type in damage → error\n23. should reject claim with negative damage amount and exit with non-zero status -- amount: -200 → error\n24. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event -- sword damage 500 G → payout 400 G\n25. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event for components -- rune damage 200 G → payout 100 G\n26. should apply 50% reimbursement for items with enchantment level ≥ 8 -- dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\n27. should fully reimburse dragon-material items -- dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G → payout 700 G\n28. should apply both dragon-material and high-enchantment rules with dragon-material winning -- dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\n29. should verify damage entries match insured items -- two sword damages but only one sword insured → reject claim\n30. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum -- sword insured (cap 2000 G), first claim 1500 G → second claim max 600 G\n31. should maintain cap exhaustion across claims -- first claim 1400 G, cap remaining 600 G; second claim 600 G, cap remaining 0 G\n"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop